{"name":"June Vision","hex":"#f1f1da","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"june","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rush."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/june"},{"term":"vision","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sense or ability of sight.","Something seen; an object perceived visually."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To imagine something as if it were to be true.","To present as in a vision."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vision"}],"entries":[{"title":"June","blocks":[{"text":"June is the sixth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars—the latter the most widely used calendar in the world. Its length is 30 days. June succeeds May and precedes July. This month marks the start of summer in the Northern Hemisphere and contains the summer solstice, which is the day with the most daylight hours. In the Southern Hemisphere, June is the start of winter and contains the winter solstice, the day with the fewest hours of daylight out of the year."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG/330px-Statue_de_Junon%2C_Louvre%2C_Ma_485%2C_trois_quarts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June","wikidata":"Q120"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png/330px-Chronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration for the month of June, based on the Calendar of Filocalus (AD 354)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChronography_of_354_Mensis_Iunius.png"},{